  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Fair weather this weekend will give way to more\nunsettled weather into early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure builds in through the weekend, with drier weather\nand more seasonable temperatures returning to the forecast \narea. Mostly sunny skies are expected today with temperatures \n1-2 degrees warmer than yesterday over most of the area. By \nSunday, cloud cover will slowly increase once more ahead of the \nnext approaching low pressure system in return flow with hipres \nbuilding to our south and east. Have cooled temps over Downeast \nwith seabreeze developing in the afternoon. \n\nThe next low pressure system to cross the area Sunday night\nthrough Monday night will be in the form of a cold front which \nbrings another round of rain and chance for thunderstorms. \nLatest guidance shows a triple point low pressure developing \nwell off the coast near Cape Cod that moves NNE into the Gulf of\nMaine. Models differ, however, on the strength and track of \nthis developing low, either closer to or farther from the \ncoast. Current thinking is that the front moves through the \nnorth bringing more showers, while Downeast and coastal areas \ncould see more steady rain from the developing system. Current \nrainfall totals range from 0.25-0.5 inches areawide with some \nlocations seeing up to 0.75 inches in heavier showers or in rain\nbands, depending on the track of the low. This system will need\nto be monitored as models come in to better agreement on the \ntrack, which could shift rainfall totals. \n\nAnother chance for rain returns Wednesday night.",
